CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ assertion \*p == 0: FAILURE$
--
--
Checks that a read through a pointer counts as a read of the variables it may
point to: `t` holds the value of the previous iteration when it is read
through `p`, so it is not a loop local and is havoced.
